From 304c6fd2ea6a968722816154bb9b3befdc45491a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:58:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] firstaid: \caption* with the float package

float.sty (frozen since 2001, loaded by many documents for [H] and by
algorithm.sty) replaces \caption by a definition that does not know the
star, so \caption*{Text} gave "Figure 2: *" with a list entry, followed
by "Text".

The first aid (applied only to float.sty v1.3d, and only if the kernel
has the caption interface, i.e. \@kernel@caption is defined, which it is
not after a roll-back) keeps float's \caption for numbered captions and
lets \caption* use the kernel definition \@kernel@caption*. For a type
restyled by float, \@caption is set for this one caption to float's
caption code \@float@c@<type>, which restores the previous \@caption and
continues. That code uses \fnum@<type> and \ext@<type> as the kernel
did, and its style macros put the label in a group ({\@fs@cfont #1:} #2,
{\@fs@cfont #1} #2), which the look-ahead of \@caption@nolabel (previous
commit) handles. So with the kernel's settings for a replaced \@caption
the caption has the style of float (ruled, plain, boxed) without label,
separator and list entry, and float's optional argument after the
caption still works.

Those settings last until the next \caption, which here can be float's
own: float's \caption (without star) therefore first runs
\@kernel@caption@reset. Otherwise a numbered caption after \caption* in
the same float lost its label and its list entry, although the counter
was stepped, and its \label got the target name of the \caption* (with
hyperref loaded before float also a duplicate destination); this
happened in restyled floats, \newfloat types, algorithm.sty, and in
plain figures when hyperref is loaded before float.

Not covered: hyperref without \DocumentMetadata loaded after float
replaces \caption again (as for all floats). The caption package
replaces \caption anyway.

Documentation: ltfloat.dtx mentions the first aid; base/changes.txt has
an item for it.

Tests: required/firstaid firstaid-float-caption (not restyled figure,
ruled table, numbered caption unchanged, optional argument of float,
numbered caption after \caption* in a restyled table, a figure, a
\newfloat type and a \restylefloat* type) and
firstaid-float-caption-hyperref (hyperref loaded before float; a
separate file because the package order differs).

The hook dumps of 15 lthooks and 2 lthooks2 tests list the new code for
package/float/after; their .tlg files are updated (additions only).
